{"id":"n1-231","title":"～ぶって","romaji":"〜butte","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Te-form of ～ぶる, meaning 'acting/pretending to be ~'.","longExplanation":"～ぶる (in te-form: ～ぶって) indicates 'behaving as if one were ~.' This is often used negatively to criticize someone for putting on airs or pretending to know more than they do (e.g., 知ったかぶって 'to act like a know-it-all').","formation":"Noun/Adjective + ぶる → ぶって (te-form)","examples":[{"jp":"彼は何でも知ったかぶって話をする。","romaji":"Kare wa nandemo shittaka butte hanashi o suru.","en":"He talks as if he knows everything.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"何でも","vocabId":"1611030","reading":"なにでも"},{"surface":"知った","vocabId":"1420470","reading":"しった","baseForm":"知る"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ぶっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ぶつ"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話をする","vocabId":"2078760","reading":"はなしをする"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5,6]},{"jp":"彼女は何も知らないふりをしてぶっていたが、本当は全部わかっている。","romaji":"Kanojo wa nanimo shiranai furi o shite butte ita ga, hontou wa zenbu wakatte iru.","en":"She was acting like she didn’t know anything, but in reality, she understands it all.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"何も","vocabId":"1188490","reading":"なにも"},{"surface":"知らないふり","vocabId":"2235450","reading":"しらないふり"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ぶっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ぶつ"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"本当は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"全部","vocabId":"1396130","reading":"ぜんぶ"},{"surface":"わかっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"わかる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId"